.\" sliverd(8). Prose: docs/sliverd.md, docs/api.md section 6, docs/safe-swap.md.
.TH SLIVERD 8 2026-10-12 "sliver 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sliverd \- Touch Bar system daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sliverd
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.br
.B sliverd \-\-fake\-hardware
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-uid
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-frame\-png
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-touch\-socket
.IR path ]
.RI [ panel ]
.br
.B sliverd \-\-headless
.I out.png
.RB [ \-\-fn ]
.RI [ panel ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sliverd
owns the Touch Bar of Apple Silicon and Intel T2 MacBook Pros: the display, the touch digitizer, the bar's backlight, and the virtual keyboard that sends its key presses.
It replaces
.BR tiny\-dfr .
.PP
The daemon is small and doesn't know about apps, configuration or widgets.
The logged\-in user's
.BR sliver\-agent (1)
renders frames and sends them over a local socket, together with the rectangles that are keys.
Only an agent owned by the user of the active session on seat0 may drive the bar.
.B sliverd
treats everything the agent sends as untrusted, and it never emits SysRq.
.PP
When no agent is driving the bar,
.B sliverd
shows its built\-in layers: F1\(enF12 normally and tiny\-dfr's media row while Fn is held (swapped with
.BR media_layer_default ).
Esc comes first on bars without a physical Escape key.
.SS Safe hatch
Press Fn twice (within 400\ ms) and keep holding it.
As long as Fn stays down,
.B sliverd
shows its built\-in F\-key layer, whatever the agent, the configuration or any app is doing.
Nothing can configure or disable this.
It is how Escape and the F\-keys stay reachable even when a configuration has removed them.
.SS Power
The display is dimmed after 30\ s without activity and turned off after 60\ s, unless the agent sets other values.
It is off while the lid is closed.
The first touch on a dark bar only wakes it.
With nothing to do, the daemon sleeps without timers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Listen here when not socket\-activated.
The default is
.I /run/sliver/sliverd.sock
(mode 0666, because each connection is authorised by its uid).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Configuration file.
The default is
.IR /etc/sliver/sliverd.toml .
.TP
.BR \-\-backend " " real | fake
Use the real hardware (the default) or the fake hardware.
.TP
.B \-\-fake\-hardware
Development mode: serve the real IPC socket, but with fake hardware.
.TP
.BI \-\-uid " n"
Fake mode: the uid treated as the active session (default: your own).
.TP
.BI \-\-frame\-png " path"
Fake mode: rewrite this PNG every time the panel is flushed.
.TP
.BI \-\-touch\-socket " path"
Fake mode: take injected input on this Unix datagram socket, one command per line:
.BI tap " x",
.BI down " x \fR[\fPslot\fR]\fP",
.BI move " x \fR[\fPslot\fR]\fP",
.BR up " [\fIslot\fP]",
.BR cancel " [\fIslot\fP]",
.BR "fn down" | up ,
.BR activity ,
.BR "lid open" | closed ,
.BR screen\-backlight .
.I x
is in bar pixels from the left edge. Touches go through the real touch path (key regions, the
agent, the hatch). For example:
.B printf 'tap 80\en' | socat \- UNIX\-SENDTO:\fIpath\fP
.TP
.BI \-\-headless " out.png"
Render what the panel would show with no agent connected, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-fn
With
.BR \-\-headless :
render the Fn layer.
.TP
.BI \-\-exit\-after " seconds"
Exit cleanly after this long (the safe\-swap test harness uses it).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log every input, agent message, state change and key press.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.PP
.I panel
options describe the hardware for fake and headless runs:
.BI \-\-width " px"
(default 2008),
.BI \-\-model " name"
(default Mac14,7),
.BI \-\-max\-brightness " n"
(default 255).
.SH HARDWARE
.B sliverd
finds the bar's devices itself, the same way
.B tiny\-dfr
does:
.TP
Display
The DRM card driven by
.B adp
(Apple Silicon) or
.B appletbdrm
(Intel T2).
Frames are drawn into a dumb buffer and only the changed columns are flushed.
.TP
Touch
The evdev device whose name contains
.RB \(lq " Touch Bar" \(rq,
read as multi\-touch protocol B.
Fingers already on the bar when
.B sliverd
starts are ignored until they lift.
.TP
Backlight
The bar's own backlight
.RI ( 228600000.dsi.0 ,
.I display\-pipe
or
.IR appletb_backlight ).
Brightness 0 is how the bar is turned off: turning the display pipe off does not blank the panel.
If the backlight can't be written (normally because udev hasn't applied
.I 99\-z\-sliverd.rules
yet),
.B sliverd
exits so that systemd can retry and then fall back to
.BR tiny\-dfr ,
which can still dim the OLED.
Only when tiny\-dfr isn't installed does it run at a fixed brightness, with a warning.
.TP
Keys
A uinput keyboard named
.RB \(lq "Sliver Touch Bar Keys" \(rq,
which the compositor treats like any other keyboard (the user's layout applies).
.PP
Devices that come and go (suspend, driver reloads) are picked up through udev.
.PP
Never test a development build by stopping
.B tiny\-dfr
by hand.
Use the safe\-swap harness
.RI ( docs/safe\-swap.md ),
which bounds the run and always gives the bar back.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I /etc/sliver/sliverd.toml
is optional.
Unknown keys and parse errors only produce warnings, and the daemon always starts.
.TP
.BR physical_esc " = " true | false
Override the guess.
Bars at least 2170\ px long are assumed to have no physical Escape key.
.TP
.BR media_layer_default " = " true | false
Built\-in layers: show media keys normally and the F\-keys while Fn is held.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/sliver/sliverd.sock
The agent socket.
.TP
.I /etc/sliver/sliverd.toml
Daemon configuration.
.TP
.I sliverd.service\fR, \fPsliverd.socket
The systemd units
.RI ( sliver.service
is an alias for
.IR sliverd.service ).
.B sliverd
runs as a dynamic user in the
.B video
and
.B input
groups.
It is restarted after a crash.
After five crashes in a minute it gives way to
.BR tiny\-dfr.service .
.TP
.I 99\-z\-sliverd.rules
The udev rule that starts
.B sliverd
for the Touch Bar devices in place of
.BR tiny\-dfr .
The package applies it to the existing bar card and backlight when it is installed, so no reboot
is needed before the first
.BR "systemctl start sliverd" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SLIVER_LOG=debug
Same as
.BR \-v .
.TP
.BR SLIVER_SAFESWAP ", " SLIVER_OUT_DIR ", " SLIVER_SAFESWAP_SECONDS
Set by the safe\-swap harness for bounded hardware test runs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sliver\-agent (1),
.BR sliverctl (1),
.BR sliver\-config (5),
.BR systemd.socket (5)
.PP
.IR docs/sliverd.md ,
.I docs/hardware.md
and
.I docs/safe\-swap.md
in the sliver sources.
